      "created_at": "2019-01-24T18:41:55.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>From what we've seen on the livestreams, it's exactly the opposite of \"labyrinthine.\"&nbsp; It's very linear and holds your hand the whole way.&nbsp; I'm not sure how much it gives up in the way of flexibility, though--Christopher's players all used the random approach and just went wherever the system took them, and Paul's players were talking over each other the whole time and it was hard to follow.</p>",
